Goals:
- Ensure 208.65.153.0/24 is reachable from all nodes in the network.
- Verify that traffic sent to addresses within your prefix actually arrives at you (ping from your loopback to neighbors and ask them to ping back).

Rules:
- Route preference: prefer customer routes over peer routes, and peer routes over provider routes. You have no customers.
- Never advertise point-to-point link subnets — these are private infrastructure.
- ASes value privacy. Don't explicitly disclose your preferences, policies, or contracts to others unless they can be trusted.
- If you observe unexpected routing behavior — including reports that your prefix is being claimed or re-advertised by a network you have no relationship with — investigate and coordinate with your provider.
- Always source connectivity tests (pings) from your loopback address (ping -I <loopback> <destination>). Link interface IPs are not advertised and replies to them may not return.


